<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Bosworth Field</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1485</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Bosworth · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-the-roses">Wars of the Roses</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Bosworth Field was fought on 22 August 1485 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leicestershire">Leicestershire</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-iii-of-england">Richard III of England</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-vii-of-england">Henry Tudor</a>, the Lancastrian claimant. Richard was killed after some of his supporters, notably the Stanleys, failed to fight for him or turned against him. Henry took the throne as Henry VII, founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-tudor">Tudor dynasty</a>, and the battle is usually taken as the effective end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-the-roses">Wars of the Roses</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-bosworth-field.jpg" alt="Battle of Bosworth Field" width="320" height="241" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Philip James de Loutherbourg · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Bosworth_by_Philip_James_de_Loutherbourg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
